Just an idea for Nethack that would involve way too much work for anyone 
who's up to code it. Not entirely serious here. Plus it's derivative of 
other games.

Simply put, some bits of armor would have sockets. One could put specific 
gems in those sockets to gain various benefits or intrinsics while wearing 
that armor. X amount of rubies in a socketed plate mail would confer fire 
resistance. Elven mithril coats bearing dilithium crystals would increase 
the caster's MP and reduce hunger. And so on and so on and so on.

Since cash from shopkeepers is limited and by the time they can only offer 
store credit they don't have much left that is worth buying.

Priests don't accept identified gems in lieu of gold for their various 
benefits (that could be a YANI). In the end, they're just good for boosting 
luck with unicorns and increasing one's score at the end of a long slog 
through the Dungeons of Doom.


